description: Par-cook your brats/sausages with steam instead of boiling to retain the full flavor of the sausages.
---

> Note that this recipe page is incomplete.
> Add details for other types of sausages.

= Preparation = 

Position a wire rack on the lowest position of the #Convection Steam Oven{} (CSO).
Position the modular rack in the frame above it, with enough clearance for a shallow pan.
Preheat the oven to 375°F on Convection Steam mode.

Preheat a charcoal or gas #grill or #Blackstone griddle{} on medium-high.

In a solid pan or shallow dish, pour in @beer{12%oz}(any flavor).
Add in @onion{1}(sliced). Optionally add @garlic{}(diced), @bay leaf{}, @peppercorns, or other aromatics.

> The CSO does not absorb liquid flavor into the food the way simmering does.
> Steam condenses vapor on the surface, so beer in the pan adds aroma, not strong
> beer flavor. Other spices in the liquid help aromatics.
> The brat's moisture and texture benefit the most.

= Meats (as desired) = 

After preheating, place the @bratwurst{4}(uncooked), @chicken sausages{4}(pre-cooked), or other sausages on a #perforated pan{} on the top of the modular rack.

Cook ~{12-18%minutes}, until brats or firm and internally over 150°F.

Finish the meats on the preheated grill or griddle to crisp the outside casing.
Cook to a safe internal temperature (165°F for bratwurst or chicken sausages).

= Serving =

Serve the sausages with your favorite @condiments and @buns.
